Package: TransmitTestandCull
Type: Package
Title: Stochastic Disease Transmission Simulation Model With Application Of A Diagnostic Test At Defined Times And Subsequent Culling
Version: 1.0.0
Date: 2025-03-11
Author: David Ewing
Maintainer: David Ewing <david.ewing@bioss.ac.uk>
Description: The function simulates a stochastic SEIR disease transmission model with gamma distributed latent and infectious periods. At pre-defined times a diagnostic test is applied with sensitivity and specificity inputted by the user. Following testing all positive animals are culled. The population is restocked to the initial population size at regular predefined intervals.
License: MIT
Imports: 
    Rcpp (>= 1.0.12),
    ggplot2,
    dplyr,
    tidyr
LinkingTo: Rcpp
URL: https://github.com/davewi13/TransmitTestandCull
BugReports: https://github.com/davewi13/TransmitTestandCull/issues
